# Placeholders, not values. install/lib/caddy.sh substitutes {{DOMAIN}},
# {{APP_NAME}} and {{UPSTREAM}} from the arguments install.sh was given.
#
# These used to be literal hostnames, and caddy_add_site prefers a committed
# snippet over the generic template — so the --domain you passed was used for the
# preflight and the public URL and then silently ignored for the site itself. A
# box would serve, and request a certificate for, whatever this file said.
#
# Generated by install/lib/caddy.sh — edit caddy/snippets/_template.caddy, not this.
#
# Committed as a worked example of what a rendered app snippet looks like. On a real
# Server B this file is produced by:
#   install.sh --app finance --domain finance.johnny.dev --upstream 127.0.0.1:8090
{{DOMAIN}} {
	import common {{APP_NAME}}

	reverse_proxy {{UPSTREAM}} {
		import streaming
	}
}
